### ===========================================================
###  Solver under pressure
###
###  Every request carries the token by hand.
###  The HTTP Client reads Max-Age as milliseconds, so the cookie expires
###  after 28 seconds instead of 8 hours.
###  https://youtrack.jetbrains.com/issue/IJPL-208287
###
###  Two cases:
###    A. not enough people, so slots have to stay empty
###    B. a position nobody is allowed to cover
###
###  Both come back 0hard. Leaving a slot empty costs medium, which is
###  cheaper than any hard penalty, and the manual rules never pin an
###  assignment that breaks a hard rule.
###
###  The weeks here are built on top of the seed, so the week of 23 Aug
###  holds shifts 64 to 84 and the week of 30 Aug holds 85 to 105. Each
###  day runs morning, evening, night.
###
###  HOW TO RUN
###  Rebuild the database:
###      docker compose down -v
###      docker compose up -d      (wait for healthy)
###      restart the app           (Flyway rebuilds the schema on startup)
###  Send the requests one at a time, because a full run of the file
###  ignores the waits that the STOP notes ask for.
### ===========================================================


### 1 Log in as manager
# @name 1 Log in as manager
POST http://localhost:8080/api/auth/login
Content-Type: application/json

{"username": "dana@shiftscheduler.local", "password": "password123"}

> {%
    if (response.status === 200) {
        const cookie = response.headers.valueOf("Set-Cookie");
        client.global.set("token", cookie.split(";")[0].split("=")[1]);
    }
%}


### ===========================================================
### A — NOT ENOUGH PEOPLE
### A week asks for 26 support agents across its shifts. Six shifts a
### week is a hard rule, so five agents can cover it and two cannot.
### ===========================================================

### A1 Stand Omer down — expect 204
# @name A1 Stand Omer down — expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/4?version=0
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### A2 Stand Shira down — expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/5?version=0
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### A3 Stand Noa down — expect 204
DELETE http://localhost:8080/api/employees/7?version=0
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### A4 Who is left — expect 200 and six active
###    Maya and Eitan are the only support agents still working
GET http://localhost:8080/api/employees
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### A5 Create the week of 23 Aug — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"weekStart": "2026-08-23"}

### A6 Lock it — expect 200, status DRAFT
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0}

### A7 Solve — expect 200
###    The log should end with something close to:
###      score 0hard/-95medium/-78soft, 24 new assignments,
###      14 slots left empty
###    Two agents can work twelve shifts between them and the week wants
###    twenty-six, so fourteen have nowhere to go. None of that is hard:
###    an empty slot costs medium, and the solver never pays a hard
###    penalty to avoid it.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/solve
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### A8 Coverage — expect 200, 24 of 38 filled
###    The gaps sit on thirteen different shifts rather than piling onto
###    a few, because an empty slot costs the same wherever it is
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/coverage
Cookie: access_token={{token}}


### A9 Status — expect 200. Keep sending it until solving comes back
###    false, then carry on.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/4/solve-status
Cookie: access_token={{token}}


### ===========================================================
###  STOP. Wait 40 seconds before carrying on, because that is how long
###  the solver is given.
### ===========================================================

### ===========================================================
### B — A POSITION NOBODY CAN COVER
### Everyone back at work, and every support agent says they cannot
### work one particular night. The night asks for one agent.
### ===========================================================

### B1 Bring Omer back — expect 200
# @name B1 Bring Omer back — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/4/activate?version=1
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### B2 Bring Shira back — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/5/activate?version=1
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### B3 Bring Noa back — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/employees/7/activate?version=1
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### B4 Create the week of 30 Aug — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"weekStart": "2026-08-30"}

### B5 Read the shift ids — expect 200, 85 to 105
###    87 is the night of 30 Aug, and it asks for one support agent
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/5
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### B6 Maya can't work it — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 87, "type": "CANNOT", "employeeId": 3}

### B7 Omer can't either — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 87, "type": "CANNOT", "employeeId": 4}

### B8 Shira — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 87, "type": "CANNOT", "employeeId": 5}

### B9 Eitan — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 87, "type": "CANNOT", "employeeId": 6}

### B10 Noa, the last of them — expect 201
POST http://localhost:8080/api/shift-preferences
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"shiftId": 87, "type": "CANNOT", "employeeId": 7}

### B11 Lock the week — expect 200
PUT http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/5/lock
Content-Type: application/json
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

{"version": 0}

### B12 Solve — expect 200
###    The log should end with something close to:
###      score 0hard/-10medium/-81soft, 37 new assignments,
###      1 slots left empty
###    Every other slot is filled. The one that is not is the night
###    nobody is allowed to work.
POST http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/5/solve
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### B13 Status — expect 200. Keep sending it until solving comes back
###     false, then read the coverage below.
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/5/solve-status
Cookie: access_token={{token}}

### ===========================================================
###  STOP. Wait 40 seconds before reading the coverage below, because that
###  is how long the solver is given.
### ===========================================================

### B14 Coverage — expect 200, 37 of 38 filled
###    Shift 87 comes back asking for one support agent with nobody on
###    it, and the position is marked essential, so the grid shows it red
# @name B14 Coverage — expect 200, 37 of 38 filled
GET http://localhost:8080/api/schedules/5/coverage
Cookie: access_token={{token}}
